    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7b22ae63_cbaad9d1",
        "filename": "voltha/adapters/brcm_openomci_onu/omci/brcm_tp_service_specific_task.py",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 247,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000480
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-19T21:30:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This logic is a little naive. The PriorityQueue MEs are not an arbitrary pool of queues. They are statically mapped to TCONT/UNI and Priority by artificact of the \"Related Port\" attribute. Since priority level and tcont/uni are allocated in Tech Profile, this logic needs to search and find the exact matching ME rather than simply popping off the first available. The pop() will only work for the first TCONT and first UNI.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 247,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 247,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "fd1049821eb81416cd69ae628d7cdc6f1b11a45e",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bbd8d1a9_e59f295b",
        "filename": "voltha/adapters/brcm_openomci_onu/omci/brcm_tp_service_specific_task.py",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 263,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000480
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-19T21:30:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The logically separated up/dn-stream GEMs need to be recombined here to configure only a single \"bi-directional\" gem to add_to_hardware that specifies the ul_prior_q as the \"Traffic Management Pointer Upstream\" and the dl_prior_q as the \"Priority Queue Pointer Downstream\".",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 263,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 263,
        "endChar": 12
      },
      "revId": "fd1049821eb81416cd69ae628d7cdc6f1b11a45e",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
